# CompanionCare

A pet care management application built with React, Vite, Firebase, and Node.js.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js (v14 or higher)
- npm or yarn
- Firebase account
- Cloudinary account

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Davidyili230/CompanionCare.git
cd CompanionCare
```

### 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
cd server && npm install && cd ..
```

### 3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root with the following variables:

```env
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_project.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_sender_id
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=your_measurement_id
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloudinary_cloud_name
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=your_unsigned_upload_preset
```

Replace each value with your actual credentials from Firebase and Cloudinary. (Get it from contributors)

## Running the Project

### Development Mode

```bash
npm run dev
```

The application will start at `http://localhost:5173`

### Build for Production

```bash
npm run build
```

## Features

- Pet profile management
- Health reminder system
- Community forum
- Pet adoption listings
- Nutrition tracking
- Supplement recommendations
